<div class="box">
<h2>Integrate this store</h2>
<p>Your public key (safe to publish - it identifies your store, it can't move funds or read your data):</p>
<pre>{{public_key}}</pre>

{{#if is_woocommerce}}
<p>This store is already connected via the WooCommerce plugin - nothing further to configure there.
Need to connect a second WordPress site to this same store? From that site's plugin settings, click
<strong>Connect</strong>, then choose <strong>use an existing store</strong> and pick this one.</p>
{{else}}
<p><strong>WooCommerce</strong> - the easiest path if your store runs WooCommerce:</p>
<ol class="steps">
<li>Install the <code>moneropay-cloud</code> plugin from your WordPress admin.</li>
<li>Go to <strong>WooCommerce &rarr; Settings &rarr; Payments &rarr; MoneroPay</strong> and click <strong>Connect</strong>.</li>
<li>Choose <strong>use an existing store</strong> and pick this one - no keys to paste in again.</li>
</ol>
{{/if}}

<p><strong>Widget embed</strong> - paste this where you want a "Pay with Monero" button on any static page:</p>
<pre>&lt;button id="moneropay-buy-button"&gt;Pay with Monero&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;div id="moneropay-checkout"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;script src="/static/moneropay-client.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script&gt;
document.getElementById('moneropay-buy-button').addEventListener('click', function () {
  MoneroPay.createOrder({
    publicKey: '{{public_key}}',
    fiatAmount: 9.99,                         // replace with the real amount
    fiatCurrency: 'USD',
  }).then(function (order) {
    MoneroPay.mount('#moneropay-checkout', order, {
      onPaid: function () { /* e.g. window.location = '/thank-you.html'; */ },
    });
  });
});
&lt;/script&gt;</pre>
<p class="hint">The script infers this instance's own address from its own <code>&lt;script src&gt;</code> - paste it
verbatim, from wherever this dashboard is hosted.</p>

<p><strong>Direct API integration</strong> - create an order against this same MoneroPay Cloud instance
(not the underlying engine - this instance owns pricing and the checkout page) and redirect the buyer to the
returned checkout link:</p>
<pre>POST /pay/{{public_key}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fiat_currency": "USD",
  "fiat_amount": "25.00"
}</pre>
<p class="hint">Send this request to wherever this dashboard is hosted (the same origin this page is on). The
response includes a <code>payment_id</code> - send the buyer to
<code>/pay/{{public_key}}/orders/&lt;payment_id&gt;</code> (same origin) to complete the payment. This endpoint
needs no secret - it's safe to call directly from your storefront's backend.</p>
</div>
